WEBVTT

1
00:00:05.634 --> 00:00:13.999
"Are we there yet?"

2
00:00:14.459 --> 00:00:15.159
Gliss complained.

3
00:00:15.179 --> 00:00:17.841
"We've been walking forever!"

4
00:00:18.642 --> 00:00:22.984
It was the following morning, but Darb still hadn't told his friends what his idea was.

5
00:00:23.725 --> 00:00:25.526
He'd said it would be easier to show them.

6
00:00:26.266 --> 00:00:31.161
After a quick breakfast of glowberries and rainwater, he'd led them on a long walk through the swamp

7
00:00:31.241 --> 00:00:32.942
and the thick forest east of town.

8
00:00:33.663 --> 00:00:38.325
Eventually the trees had thinned out into an area of small farms and open land.

9
00:00:38.345 --> 00:00:41.087
"We're almost there," Darb said.

10
00:00:41.107 --> 00:00:44.248
"You'll see it as soon as we get to the top of the next hill."

11
00:00:44.989 --> 00:00:46.109
He led the way up the hill.

12
00:00:46.790 --> 00:00:50.272
When Zann caught up to Darb, he saw a farm spread out beneath them.

13
00:00:50.992 --> 00:00:53.914
It had several paddocks full of large, grazing dragons!

14
00:00:53.934 --> 00:00:57.756
"There," Darb said with a smile, pointing to the dragons.

15
00:00:58.464 --> 00:01:00.105
"That's how we can get to First City."

16
00:01:00.125 --> 00:01:03.908
"But I don't know how to ride a dragon," Gliss exclaimed.

17
00:01:03.928 --> 00:01:06.210
"I don't either," Perda said.

18
00:01:06.230 --> 00:01:10.793
"I begged for lessons, but my parents wanted me to focus on my spells."

19
00:01:10.813 --> 00:01:14.836
"I started learning last year after I left school," Darb said.

20
00:01:14.856 --> 00:01:18.899
"I come here a lot and help the farmer with his work in exchange for lessons."

21
00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:21.061
Zann was surprised.

22
00:01:21.741 --> 00:01:25.064
He'd never thought much about what his friend did while everyone else was in school.

23
00:01:25.760 --> 00:01:28.321
Who could have guessed that Darb was learning to ride dragons?

24
00:01:28.961 --> 00:01:30.802
Darb hurried off to talk to the farmer.

25
00:01:31.723 --> 00:01:35.004
Moments later he was back with permission to borrow two dragons.

26
00:01:35.024 --> 00:01:39.546
"We can ride double," he said as they entered the closest paddock.

27
00:01:40.206 --> 00:01:41.206
He smiled at Gliss.

28
00:01:41.226 --> 00:01:44.528
"If you want to ride with me, I can show you the best ways to hold on."

29
00:01:44.548 --> 00:01:47.849
"Oh!" Gliss shot Zann an uncertain look.

30
00:01:48.189 --> 00:01:49.430
"Um, okay.

31
00:01:49.770 --> 00:01:54.312
Thanks." "Guess that means I'm stuck with you," Perda told Zann with a shrug.

32
00:01:55.100 --> 00:01:56.121
Zann didn't answer.

33
00:01:56.461 --> 00:02:00.745
For one thing, the thought of riding double with Perda made him feel weirdly nervous.

34
00:02:01.485 --> 00:02:03.787
For another, they'd just reached the dragons.

35
00:02:04.828 --> 00:02:06.369
One of the huge creatures looked up.

36
00:02:07.090 --> 00:02:10.653
It had large, gentle eyes and iridescent purple scales.

37
00:02:11.493 --> 00:02:13.575
Zing scurried over to sniff its nose.

38
00:02:14.315 --> 00:02:18.899
When Zing let out a tiny burst of flame, the bigger dragon jumped back in surprise.

39
00:02:18.919 --> 00:02:21.661
"Behave, Zing," Zann warned.

40
00:02:21.681 --> 00:02:24.764
"Otherwise Darb will tell these guys to eat you."

41
00:02:25.452 --> 00:02:28.014
"They don't eat anything but plants—they're cloud gliders."

42
00:02:28.814 --> 00:02:30.675
Darb patted one of the large dragons.

43
00:02:31.756 --> 00:02:35.738
"Their owner thinks they'll be easier to handle than the wind racers even though they're not quite as

44
00:02:35.778 --> 00:02:40.702
fast." He gestured at several larger, fiercer-looking dragons in the next paddock.

45
00:02:40.722 --> 00:02:43.243
"I'll take his word for it."

46
00:02:43.984 --> 00:02:46.365
Zann stared up at the nearest cloud glider.

47
00:02:47.085 --> 00:02:50.908
Was he really about to climb onto this huge creature and soar into the air?

48
00:02:51.748 --> 00:02:56.929
Once again he found himself thinking that having adventures was a lot scarier than he'd ever expected.

49
00:02:58.070 --> 00:03:01.071
Still, he wasn't about to let the girls see that he was nervous.

50
00:03:01.091 --> 00:03:03.491
"What are we waiting for?"

51
00:03:03.831 --> 00:03:04.432
he exclaimed.

52
00:03:04.772 --> 00:03:05.332
"Let's go!"

53
00:03:06.132 --> 00:03:08.993
Grabbing the cloud glider's wing, he vaulted onto its back.

54
00:03:09.793 --> 00:03:13.594
The dragon gave a snort of surprise and leaped straight into the air.

55
00:03:14.014 --> 00:03:15.395
Zann tumbled to the ground.

56
00:03:15.415 --> 00:03:17.875
"Zann!" Gliss exclaimed.

57
00:03:17.895 --> 00:03:19.136
"Are you okay?"

58
00:03:19.156 --> 00:03:21.100
"I'm fine."

59
00:03:22.301 --> 00:03:23.682
Zann winced as he stood up.

60
00:03:24.963 --> 00:03:30.267
Pretty sure that a bruise was already forming on his backside, he turned to Darb with a sheepish

61
00:03:30.447 --> 00:03:34.150
smile. "Maybe you'd better give us a quick lesson."

62
00:03:35.050 --> 00:03:37.652
Darb explained how to handle and steer the dragons.

63
00:03:38.393 --> 00:03:40.514
Then he helped Zann mount the correct way.

64
00:03:40.534 --> 00:03:44.337
"Zann, you hold on to the dragon's neck," he said.

65
00:03:44.357 --> 00:03:46.438
"Perda, you hold on to Zann."

66
00:03:46.458 --> 00:03:51.221
"This is scary," Perda said as she settled into place behind Zann.

67
00:03:52.242 --> 00:03:54.983
He could feel her breath on his neck and smell her hair.

68
00:03:55.743 --> 00:03:58.964
He tried not to react as she slipped her arms around his waist.

69
00:03:59.865 --> 00:04:02.086
"You'd better hold on tight," he said.

70
00:04:02.106 --> 00:04:05.667
"I'm not jumping down to catch you if you fall off."

71
00:04:06.487 --> 00:04:06.988
She laughed.

72
00:04:07.948 --> 00:04:11.189
"I'm not the one who already fell off, remember?"

73
00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.971
By then Darb and Gliss had climbed onto the other dragon.

74
00:04:14.991 --> 00:04:17.052
"Ready?" Darb called.

75
00:04:17.332 --> 00:04:18.593
"Hang on and follow us!"

76
00:04:19.354 --> 00:04:21.055
Darb's dragon leaped into the air.

77
00:04:21.816 --> 00:04:24.198
Zann could feel his own dragon gathering its muscles.

78
00:04:24.958 --> 00:04:27.561
He held on tightly as the beast sprang upward.

79
00:04:28.261 --> 00:04:30.823
The wind from its wings rushed past Zann's head.

80
00:04:35.767 --> 00:04:37.929
flying!" Perda said with a laugh.

81
00:04:38.790 --> 00:04:39.430
Zann grinned.

82
00:04:39.991 --> 00:04:46.276
"Yeah!" Morb smiled as another red light on the map blinked off.

83
00:04:47.180 --> 00:04:48.321
"Good," he thought.

84
00:04:48.942 --> 00:04:50.463
The trolls were working fast.

85
00:04:51.203 --> 00:04:54.385
A moment later he heard a cell door slam shut in the dungeon.

86
00:04:55.106 --> 00:04:58.869
The new prisoners yelled angry protests at the trolls who had captured them.

87
00:04:58.889 --> 00:05:06.414
"If they're upset now, wait until they find out what I have planned next," he muttered with a

88
00:05:06.474 --> 00:05:11.318
cackle. His gaze fell on the discarded blink images of Zann and his friends.

89
00:05:12.138 --> 00:05:13.920
Seeing them made his good mood waver.

90
00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.082
How had a handful of puny children managed to evade him?

91
00:05:18.522 --> 00:05:19.583
It was infuriating!

92
00:05:20.283 --> 00:05:21.944
But he tried not to think about that.

93
00:05:22.765 --> 00:05:23.745
Soon it wouldn't matter.

94
00:05:24.766 --> 00:05:30.069
Turning away from the Secret Eye, Morb stepped over to a rough wooden desk and picked up a

95
00:05:30.169 --> 00:05:31.289
frayed blink image.

96
00:05:32.010 --> 00:05:33.771
It was a portrait of a large family.

97
00:05:34.431 --> 00:05:37.793
There were two handsome, smiling parents, both Reds.

98
00:05:38.914 --> 00:05:42.696
Around them were a dozen children, more than half of them Reds as well.

99
00:05:43.768 --> 00:05:47.111
But Morb's gaze barely flickered over most of the cheerful figures.

100
00:05:47.911 --> 00:05:52.555
His focus rested on an unsmiling, skinny, amber-eyed little boy.

101
00:05:53.356 --> 00:05:54.877
The family's only Void.

102
00:05:55.637 --> 00:05:59.581
Morb stared at the boy for a long moment, and then tossed the picture aside.

103
00:06:00.281 --> 00:06:02.343
He wasn't that pathetic little Void anymore.

104
00:06:04.264 --> 00:06:07.126
And soon everyone in Magica would know it.
